(*!
<summary>Beckhoff EL3403 phase input PDO with synchronization diagnostics.</summary>
<description>
Represents one EL3403 phase TxPDO (0x1A00, 0x1A01 or 0x1A02).
Status is the 16-bit PDO header: bit 13 is Sync error and bit 15 is TxPDO Toggle.
This header does not expose the EL3413/EL3433 voltage/current error flags.
Current and Voltage are signed raw values in 0.000001 A and 0.0001 V; ActivePower is in 0.01 W.
Transformer ratios and terminal variants affect scaling. VariantValue units follow acknowledged Index.
Indices 0..5 select apparent/reactive power, energy, power factor, frequency and negative energy.
Evaluate bus validity, synchronization and terminal-wide Status before using measurements.
Link fields individually; this is not a packed wire buffer. Use one owner task and synchronize other access.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE EL3403_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	Current AT %I* : DINT;
	Voltage AT %I* : DINT;
	ActivePower AT %I* : DINT;
	Index AT %I* : USINT;
	VariantValue AT %I* : DINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
